WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.362
Module 7 builds on earlier SQL ideas.

00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:09.512
You should already recognize basic SELECT queries, aggregate functions, simple joins, and NULL.

00:00:09.512 --> 00:00:13.547
Subqueries combine those familiar pieces in a new structure.

00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:17.812
If you can read a simple query on its own, the main new skill is understanding how the result of one

00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:21.037
query is used by another.

00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:26.172
Connect this idea to a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists.

00:00:26.172 --> 00:00:31.147
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.147 --> 00:00:38.092
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:43.052
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:43.052 --> 00:00:48.160
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
